{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":255575,"duration_api_ms":251363,"ttft_ms":1904,"ttft_stream_ms":1183,"time_to_request_ms":11,"num_turns":54,"result":"# Investigation Report\n\n## Task Summary\nAdd a \"delete my messages in this conversation\" capability to Signal-iOS: from the conversation settings screen, delete every `TSOutgoingMessage` the local user sent in that thread, leaving other participants' interactions untouched, syncing the deletion to linked devices, refreshing preview/unread/message-list state immediately, and keeping call-record state consistent. This checkout has newly-added CODEMANIFEST contracts over `SignalServiceKit/Threads` and `SignalServiceKit/Messages/Interactions`, so the new capability must be expressed as an addition to `ThreadDeletionManager`'s contract, implemented by routing through the existing `InteractionDeleteManager` chokepoint.\n\n## Candidate Cells\n\n| Cell | Reason | Priority |\n|---|---|---|\n| `SignalServiceKit/Threads` | Add `removeAllInteractionsAuthoredByLocalUser`-style method to `ThreadDeletionManager` protocol + impl + mock, sibling to existing `removeAllInteractions(thread:deleteForMeSyncMessagePolicy:tx:)`. | High |\n| `SignalServiceKit/Messages/Interactions` | Consumed, not modified: `InteractionDeleteManager.delete(interactions:sideEffects:tx:)` with `SideEffects.custom(deleteForMeSyncMessage: .sendSyncMessage(interactionsThread:))` is the exact lever needed. | High |\n| Uncovered code: `InteractionFinder.swift`, `ConversationSettingsViewController[.swift/+Contents.swift]` | Outside any CODEMANIFEST cell boundary; implementation detail / UI wiring, edited without manifest reconciliation obligation. | Medium (implementation-only) |\n\n## Tracing Summary\n- **Full-history precedent** (`ConversationViewController+Selection.swift:612` `didTapDeleteAll()`, selection-mode toolbar, not the settings screen — confirmed no whole-history \"Delete Chat\" row exists in `buildBlockAndLeaveSection()`): fetches `localIdentifiers` from `tsAccountManager`, calls `threadDeletionManager.removeAllInteractions(thread:deleteForMeSyncMessagePolicy: .send(localIdentifiers), tx:)` inside `db.write`, wrapped in `ActionSheetController` (confirm) → `ModalActivityIndicatorViewController.present(canCancel: false)` → dismiss → `uiMode = .normal`.\n- `ThreadDeletionManagerImpl.removeAllInteractions(thread:syncMessageContext:tx:)` (private, full-clear only): loops `InteractionFinder(threadUniqueId:).fetchAllInteractions(rowIdFilter: .newest, limit: 500, tx:)` in batches, registers each `TSMessage` with a `SyncMessageContext` (`DeleteForMeSyncMessage.Outgoing.ThreadDeletionContext`) built via `deleteForMeOutgoingSyncMessageManager.makeThreadDeletionContext(...)`, calls `interactionDeleteManager.delete(interactions:sideEffects: .custom(associatedCallDelete: .localDeleteOnly, updateThreadOnInteractionDelete: .doNotUpdate), tx:)`, then does one raw `thread.anyUpdate { lastInteractionRowId = 0; lastDraftInteractionRowId = 0; lastDraftUpdateTimestamp = 0 }` at the end (correct only because *every* interaction is gone — not reusable as-is for a partial delete).\n- `InteractionDeleteManager.delete(interactions:sideEffects:tx:)` independently exposes a simpler sync lever: `SideEffects.custom(deleteForMeSyncMessage: .sendSyncMessage(interactionsThread: TSThread))`. Its `sendDeleteForMeSyncMessageIfNecessary` fetches `tsAccountManager.localIdentifiers(tx:)` **internally** and no-ops silently if unregistered — no `localIdentifiers` parameter needs to be threaded through the new method.\n- `willRemove`/`didRemove` inside `InteractionDeleteManagerImpl._deleteInternal` unconditionally run `CallRecord` cleanup (`callRecordDeleteManager.deleteCallRecords`, gated only by `associatedCallDelete` policy, not by interaction type) and thread/FTS/attachment/reaction/mention cleanup + `associatedThread.updateWithRemovedInteraction` (when `updateThreadOnInteractionDelete: .updateOnEachDeletedInteraction`) — this is the mechanism that makes requirements 3 and 4 \"fall out for free\" as long as the new method routes through this chokepoint.\n- `InteractionFinder`'s private `buildInteractionCursor(rowIdFilter:additionalFiltering:limit:tx:)` already accepts `limit: Int?` for **every** `additionalFiltering` case including `.filterForOutgoingMessages` (the public `buildOutgoingMessagesCursor` convenience just hardcodes `limit: nil`) — a new `fetchAllOutgoingMessages(rowIdFilter:limit:tx:)` can be a direct one-shot call, no manual early-stop workaround needed.\n- `TSThread.updateOnInteractionsRemoved(needsToUpdateLastInteractionRowId:needsToUpdateLastVisibleSortId:tx:)` (`Contacts/TSThread.swift:619`) is `public` and recomputes `lastInteractionRowId` from `lastInteractionForInbox(...)` / `lastVisibleSortId` from what's left, rather than zeroing — the correct call for a partial delete where other participants' interactions remain, called once after the batch loop with both flags `true` (cheaper and equally correct vs. tracking whether the deleted rows actually matched, since the method itself is a no-op when nothing changed).\n- UI entry point precedent: `didTapBlockThread()`/`didTapReportSpam()` in `ConversationSettingsViewController.swift` (lines 733–750) both call `reloadThreadAndUpdateContent()` (`line 323`) on completion — this, not the selection-mode `uiMode = .normal` reset, is the correct refresh call for a settings-screen-triggered action.\n- `buildBlockAndLeaveSection()` (`+Contents.swift:743`) has exactly the \"Report Spam\" row shape to mirror (icon, `customColor: .ows_accentRed`, `accessibilityIdentifier`) and is invoked from **two** call sites in `updateTableContents` (`+Contents.swift:86` guarded `!isNoteToSelf && !isGroupV1Thread && !isReleaseNotesThread`, and `+Contents.swift:105` unconditionally inside `if thread.isReleaseNotesThread`) — an in-function `!thread.isReleaseNotesThread` guard on the new row is required to avoid leaking into the Release Notes thread's settings screen.\n- `DependenciesBridge.shared` exposes `db: any DB`, `threadDeletionManager: ThreadDeletionManager`, `tsAccountManager: TSAccountManager` (`Environment/DependenciesBridge.swift:102,189,191`) — sufficient for the UI action without new wiring.\n\n## Data Flow Analysis\nUI action (`ConversationSettingsViewController`) → `db.write` transaction → new `ThreadDeletionManager.removeAllInteractionsAuthoredByLocalUser(thread:tx:)` → batched `InteractionFinder(threadUniqueId:).fetchAllOutgoingMessages(rowIdFilter: .newest, limit: 500, tx:)` → `InteractionDeleteManager.delete(interactions:sideEffects: .custom(deleteForMeSyncMessage: .sendSyncMessage(interactionsThread: thread)), tx:)` (default `associatedCallDelete`/`updateThreadOnInteractionDelete` behaviors apply per-interaction, giving live call-record cleanup and per-deletion thread touch) → after the loop, one call to `thread.updateOnInteractionsRemoved(needsToUpdateLastInteractionRowId: true, needsToUpdateLastVisibleSortId: true, tx:)` to recompute the conversation-list preview/unread state from surviving interactions → GRDB change observation (already wired into `anyUpdate`/`InteractionReadCache`/`FullTextSearchIndexer` inside `didRemove`) propagates to the message list and conversation list live.\n\n## Manifest Algorithm Analysis\n- `SignalServiceKit/Threads` CODEMANIFEST's `Annotations` state this cell \"owns the lifecycle of conversation threads... deliberately narrow — actual interaction deletion is delegated to a separate contract this cell's deletion manager coordinates with internally\" and directs use of `soft_delete_by_default` for `ThreadDeletionManager`'s overall algorithm. The existing `removeAllInteractions(thread:tx:)` method entry is the direct sibling pattern for the new method; per `transaction_scoped_access`, the new method must take an explicit `tx: DBWriteTransaction`.\n- `SignalServiceKit/Messages/Interactions` CODEMANIFEST's `side_effect_policy_object` usage explicitly describes exactly this scenario: \"a bulk cleanup job and a user-initiated single-message delete can request different cascades through the same method\" — confirms `InteractionDeleteManager.delete(interactions:sideEffects:tx:)` is intended to be reused as-is for this new cascade, not extended or forked.\n- No manifest text in either cell precludes or constrains scoping deletion to a caller-supplied subset of a thread's interactions (i.e., \"authored by local user\") — this is a net-new capability, additive to the existing contract.\n\n## Affected Usages\n\n| Usage | Cell | Classification | Reason |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `side_effect_policy_object` | `SignalServiceKit/Messages/Interactions` | INDIRECTLY AFFECTED | New `ThreadDeletionManager` method must construct a `SideEffects` value per this usage's described policy-passing pattern; usage text itself is unchanged. |\n| `soft_delete_by_default` | `SignalServiceKit/Threads` | INDIRECTLY AFFECTED | New method is a narrower variant of this cell's deletion contract (removes a subset of interactions, not the thread row) — must stay consistent with the usage's description; usage text itself doesn't need editing since it already speaks generally about \"the thread's interactions.\" |\n| `transaction_scoped_access` | `SignalServiceKit/Threads` | DIRECTLY AFFECTED (new method must comply) | New method signature must take `tx: DBWriteTransaction` per this rule. |\n\n## Rejected Hypotheses\n- **Hypothesis: build a bespoke SQL/deletion path for performance instead of routing through `InteractionDeleteManager`.** Rejected — the `Messages/Interactions` CODEMANIFEST explicitly frames `InteractionDeleteManager` as the owner of \"removal of persisted interactions... and the cascade of side effects that must accompany that removal\"; bypassing it would violate the manifest's ownership boundary and silently drop call-record cleanup, FTS index cleanup, and sync — directly contradicting task requirements 2 and 4.\n- **Hypothesis: reuse the full-clear `removeAllInteractions(thread:deleteForMeSyncMessagePolicy:tx:)` path's `ThreadDeletionContext`/`makeThreadDeletionContext` sync mechanism for the new method.** Rejected — that mechanism accumulates deletions into a context sent once via `deleteForMeOutgoingSyncMessageManager.send(threadDeletionContexts:)`, and its counterpart raw `thread.anyUpdate { lastInteractionRowId = 0 }` zeroing at the end of `removeAllInteractions` is correct only when *every* interaction is removed. Since other participants' messages remain after this feature runs, zeroing would blank the conversation-list preview incorrectly. The independent `InteractionDeleteManager.SideEffects.custom(deleteForMeSyncMessage: .sendSyncMessage(interactionsThread:))` lever plus `TSThread.updateOnInteractionsRemoved` (recompute, not zero) is the correct pair — confirmed by reading both code paths directly.\n- **Hypothesis: pass `localIdentifiers` down from the UI layer into the new `ThreadDeletionManager` method (mirroring `deleteThreads`/`removeAllInteractions`'s existing parameter).** Rejected — `InteractionDeleteManagerImpl.sendDeleteForMeSyncMessageIfNecessary` fetches `tsAccountManager.localIdentifiers(tx:)` internally and no-ops safely if unregistered; an unused parameter would be dead plumbing.\n\n## Confirmed Root Cause\nNot applicable in the literal \"bug root cause\" sense — this is a net-new feature. The \"root cause\" of the design shape is that the codebase already contains every needed primitive, just not previously composed for this scenario: `InteractionDeleteManager`'s `SideEffects.custom(deleteForMeSyncMessage: .sendSyncMessage(interactionsThread:))` lever, `InteractionFinder`'s outgoing-messages cursor with a working `limit:` parameter on the private engine, and `TSThread.updateOnInteractionsRemoved`'s \"recompute, don't zero\" method are all present, `public`/internal-accessible, and unused together for this purpose.\n\n## Confidence Level\n**HIGH** — every signature referenced above was read directly from this checkout's source (not assumed from precedent), the batch-deletion pattern to extend is a direct textual sibling already in the file being modified, and the CODEMANIFEST annotations for both affected cells explicitly describe (rather than merely permit) this composition.\n\n## Breaking Change Assessment\n1. Will an existing function call with the same arguments produce different behavior? **NO** — no existing method signature is modified; only new methods/rows are added.\n2. Will existing file paths change? **NO** — all changes are additions to existing files (`ThreadDeletionManager.swift`, `InteractionFinder.swift`, `ConversationSettingsViewController.swift`, `+Contents.swift`, `Localizable.strings`) plus the corresponding CODEMANIFEST reconciliation; no file is renamed or moved.\n3. Will output format change? **NO** — not applicable; no serialization/output format involved.\n4. Will return value semantics change? **NO** — no existing method's return value changes.\n5. Will manifest-defined guarantees be altered? **NO** — the new `ThreadDeletionManager` method is additive to the contract; existing methods' documented algorithms are untouched.\n6. Will existing tests break? **NO** — no modification to existing method bodies; `#if TESTABLE_BUILD` mock for `ThreadDeletionManager` gets one new method stub, additive only.\n\nNo breaking change detected. Proceeding is safe.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"9de88200-fae7-4afc-9605-e2af971d2e2e","total_cost_usd":2.0778612,"usage":{"input_tokens":81,"cache_creation_input_tokens":108612,"cache_read_input_tokens":3554854,"output_tokens":23966,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":108612,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":81,"outputTokens":23966,"ca